<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2752" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΐτας</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ], ὁ</span>, 
			Dor.
		 word for <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a beloved
				youth</i>, answering to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσπνήλας</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴσπνηλος</span> (the lover), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				738
			</span></i> (fort. <i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				12.14
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴτης</span>, said to be a
			Thessalian word), cj. in <i><span class="en">
				23.63
			</span></i>; generally, <i>lover</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χρύσας</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθανᾶς </span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> δ᾽ ἀΐτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dosiad.
					<u>Ara</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				461
			</span></i>:—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀῖτις</span></b>  Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.105
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.296
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				125
			</span></i>.</div>
